    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d272">

                <pb facs="0488" n="386" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg386"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C114/1577: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-01-11T11:00:00+01:00">January 11,
                            1935—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 12—3:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. Department’s telegram No. 2, January 9, 5 p.m. Without stating that I was
                    acting under instructions I discussed the situation informally <pb facs="0489"
                        n="387" xml:id="pg387"/> with Avenol<anchor n="11" xml:id="d272-f1"/> who,
                    adopting the idea, will proceed with it on a personal basis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d272-f1" n="11" xml:id="d272-f1-content">
                <p>Joseph A. Avenol, Secretary General of the League of Nations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
